==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|besteln}}

===Etymology===
An [[Upper German]] verb, from earlier {{m|de|besteln}}, iterative of {{der|de|gmh|besten}}, from {{der|de|gmw-pro|*bastijan}}. The ''-a-'' is perhaps dialectal or through readaptation to the underlying noun {{m|de|Bast|t=bast}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈbastəln/|[ˈbastl̩n]}}
* {{audio|de|De-basteln.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|ambitransitive}} to perform [[handicrafts]] or [[DIY]], to build, to craft (especially something from [[paper]], [[fabric]], and related materials, by [[cut]]ting, [[fold]]ing, [[glue|gluing]], etc., e.g. such objects as [[kite]]s, [[lantern]]s, [[calendar]]s, [[greeting card]]s), 
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[tinker]] (with), to work (on) {{gloss|in an attempt to fix, mend or improve it}} {{+obj|de|:an(dat)<something>}}

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj}}

